<p>A <code>RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePickerButton</code> is one
  option inside a
  <a href="/components/red-orange-yellow-green-blue-picker/"><code>RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePicker</code></a>.
  Each button is a <code>&lt;button role="radio"&gt;</code> with
  a <code>data-status</code> attribute of
  <code>"red" | "orange" | "yellow" | "green" | "blue"</code>
  that the example CSS uses to colour the border and the selected
  background.</p>

<p>See the <a href="/components/red-orange-yellow-green-blue-picker/">Picker
  demo</a> for composed examples.</p>

{# BEGIN generated: examples (bin/generate-examples) #}
<h2>Usage</h2>
<pre tabindex="0"><code>{% raw %}&lt;RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePicker label="Risk assessment"&gt;
  &lt;RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePickerButton value="red" label="Red - Critical" onclick={handleSelect} /&gt;
  &lt;RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePickerButton value="orange" label="Orange - Serious" onclick={handleSelect} /&gt;
  &lt;RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePickerButton value="yellow" label="Yellow - Caution" selected onclick={handleSelect} /&gt;
  &lt;RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePickerButton value="green" label="Green - Good" onclick={handleSelect} /&gt;
  &lt;RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePickerButton value="blue" label="Blue - Excellent" onclick={handleSelect} /&gt;
&lt;/RedOrangeYellowGreenBluePicker&gt;
{% endraw %}</code></pre>
